==Finnish==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|fi|pohjanen|pohjaanen|pohjainen|pohjonen||dialectal}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|urj-fin-pro|*pohjainën}}, equivalent to {{suffix|fi|pohja|inen|t1=bottom, north}}. Adapted from the Savonian dialects, whence the ''-oi-'' (a regular change also seen in e.g. {{m|fi||hopioinen}} < {{m|fi|hopea}} + {{m|fi|-inen}}), and introduced into the standard language by [[w:fi:Abraham Poppius|Abraham Poppius]] in 1818.

